{
  "source": "Prompts/critical-thinking-reroll-2.mp4",
  "duration": 202.8495625,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.68,
      "text": "What you know matters, but what you do with it matters more."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.34,
      "end": 9.06,
      "text": "Baseline knowledge helps you understand a subject and recognize when things don't add up."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.62,
      "end": 14.94,
      "text": "Next is critical thinking, questioning claims, examining evidence, and considering alternatives."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.12,
      "end": 20.7,
      "text": "Combining what you know with how you think yields better questions and better decisions."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.52,
      "end": 25.0,
      "text": "Ultimately, you become smarter than the tool you're using."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.0,
      "end": 31.26,
      "text": "Success depends on the deliberate habit of asking exactly what would have to be true for a specific claim to hold up."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.12,
      "end": 36.24,
      "text": "In 2015, headlines around the world announced a delicious discovery."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.04,
      "end": 40.28,
      "text": "A new study appeared to show that eating chocolate helps you lose weight."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.12,
      "end": 43.02,
      "text": "Slim by chocolate ran one front page."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.92,
      "end": 45.12,
      "text": "Did that headline make you pause?"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.9,
      "end": 48.16,
      "text": "If it did, that's your critical thinking getting started."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.98,
      "end": 53.2,
      "text": "When people encountered that morning headline, the reactions generally went in two directions."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.2,
      "end": 57.58,
      "text": "The first was to take it at face value. Sounds great, I believe it."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.2,
      "end": 60.42,
      "text": "The second was the critical thinking reaction."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.16,
      "end": 64.16,
      "text": "Wait a second, what's the actual evidence behind this claim?"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.82,
      "end": 71.66,
      "text": "You have to force yourself to pause and investigate, especially when a claim sounds exactly what you desperately want to believe."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.4,
      "end": 76.7,
      "text": "The study was technically real, but it was designed to be mathematically flimsy."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.7,
      "end": 84.2,
      "text": "The researchers used a tiny sample size of just 15 participants, and then they tracked 18 different things about them."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.78,
      "end": 92.9,
      "text": "With that many measurements across such a small group, it is mathematically likely that at least one random chance result will look like an important discovery."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.68,
      "end": 98.2,
      "text": "To complete the setup, the research institute backing the study was just a fake website."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.96,
      "end": 101.84,
      "text": "The author was actually a journalist trying to prove a point."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.84,
      "end": 107.88,
      "text": "A poorly conducted study paired with a great headline would fly around the world before anyone checked the facts."
    },
    {
      "start": 108.58,
      "end": 109.04,
      "text": "He was right."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.66,
      "end": 117.14,
      "text": "That is why the ability to read between the lines and verify facts is a required defense against manipulative information."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.12,
      "end": 122.56,
      "text": "To avoid falling into traps, there are five habits you can build to sharpen your thinking."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.34,
      "end": 126.14,
      "text": "Each one is a question you must actively ask yourself."
    },
    {
      "start": 126.14,
      "end": 128.94,
      "text": "First, is it actually right?"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.6,
      "end": 134.1,
      "text": "You ask what specific evidence supports the claim and check if it proves the conclusion."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.12,
      "end": 136.98,
      "text": "Second, do I know enough to judge?"
    },
    {
      "start": 137.68,
      "end": 143.36,
      "text": "You have to recognize where your own knowledge ends and identify exactly what new information you need."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.18,
      "end": 145.4,
      "text": "Third, what's missing?"
    },
    {
      "start": 146.24,
      "end": 152.72,
      "text": "You actively look for omitted context, absent data, and completely different explanations for the information provided."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.3,
      "end": 155.22,
      "text": "Fourth, why am I convinced?"
    },
    {
      "start": 156.08,
      "end": 161.76,
      "text": "Question your own motives to see if you are swayed by hard evidence, confident wording, or wishful thinking."
    },
    {
      "start": 162.54,
      "end": 164.08,
      "text": "And fifth, what's my call?"
    },
    {
      "start": 164.76,
      "end": 169.96,
      "text": "Finally, you decide what to believe or do, keeping the flexibility to change your mind when you learn more."
    },
    {
      "start": 170.68,
      "end": 173.3,
      "text": "These five questions work on any information you consume."
    },
    {
      "start": 174.0,
      "end": 177.2,
      "text": "They are especially critical when you use artificial intelligence."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.94,
      "end": 184.16,
      "text": "AI can help point out a flaw in your own logic, or it can confidently repeat a hallucinated error."
    },
    {
      "start": 184.94,
      "end": 188.5,
      "text": "The burden is completely on you to judge which one of those is happening."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.32,
      "end": 193.32,
      "text": "Artificial intelligence amplifies whatever level of thought you bring to the prompt."
    },
    {
      "start": 194.28,
      "end": 199.08,
      "text": "Good critical thinking going into the tool is the only way to get sharper, reliable output."
    }
  ],
